def two_sum(nums: list[int], target: int) -> list[int]:
    num_to_index = {}
    for index, num in enumerate(nums):
        complement = target - num
        if complement in num_to_index:
            return [num_to_index[complement], index]
        num_to_index[num] = index
```

This solution uses a dictionary to keep track of the numbers we've seen so far and their indices. We check for each number whether its complement (target minus the current number) has been seen before, which allows us to find the two indices in O(n) time.

